<title>UK: UK Conservatives vow to modernise London 'tube'.</title>
<headline>UK Conservatives vow to modernise London 'tube'.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's ruling Conservative party said on Wednesday it would bring forward plans to privatise the London underground railway system and recycle the proceeds to modernise the network within five years.</p>
<p>&quot;We will bring forward plans to privatise London Underground,&quot; the party said in its manifesto for Britain's May 1 election.</p>
<p>&quot;We will regulate fares so they rise by no more than inflation for at least four years after privatisation.&quot;</p>
<p>The Conservatives said that after completing the network's modernisation, the majority of the remaining surplus from privatisation would be channeled into additional support for transport investment in London and elsewhere in Britain.</p>
</text>
